"""Derive SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.1.py from SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.0.py (the tools/deploy_set.py SET pin, generated by
tools/zones_0_3_0_patch.py - never re-run that one for this). Edit THIS patch, never the generated script. Every anchor is asserted; at the
end every change is undone on a copy and compared with 0.3.0 (tools/soundpass_gen.Patch). Line endings kept.
Run:  python tools/zones_0_3_1_patch.py   then   python SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.1.py   (never --deploy)
Harness: python SkyyZones/test_skyyzones_0.3.1.py [--keep]

0.3.1 = SkyyZones 0.3 step 2 (research/cloud/SkyyZones-0.3-Spec.md sections 3.1 - 3.4, 4, 6.3, 6.4, 7 B1-B7) on the live pin 0.3.0, plus the
zones03 finisher's follow-ups (docs/log/2026-10.md 2026-10-24 "PINNED zones03" line).
Skyy's words: 2026-10-15 "placing is limited to a few things like scaffolding that vanishes after a few seconds" (docs/answered/world.md 75);
2026-10-20 spec defaults "break gate Iron 10 / Thorium-Cobalt 20 / Adamantite 30 / Mithril 40; ... anti-AFK 15 min + 300 breaks/min;
contested limit 120 / 10 min; ... scaffolding only 8 s x 24 with the item" (world.md 120); 2026-10-20 "just go with the recommended on all
of them" = every [default] of the spec's Questions for Skyy: Q1 keep the locked gate numbers, Q2 Scaffolding is crafted at the Workbench
(4 sticks -> 8), Q7 scaffolding may hang over the void edge (24 blocks that vanish after 8 s cannot reach another island).
 1. SCAFFOLDING (Z3b, spec 6.3): a new item + block Skyy_Scaffold "Scaffolding" (vanilla first: Assets.zip has NO scaffold / lattice /
    trellis block - checked again at every build; fixer: also searched ladder / platform / fence platform: the ~20 Furniture_*_Ladder
    items are wall-mounted climb models (HitboxType Ladder), the Furniture_*_Platform items need wall Support (shelf platforms), the
    Prototype fence platforms are trapdoor hitboxes, Trap_Ancient_Platform is a trap - none is a free-standing block to pillar / bridge
    with, so they are not scaffolding (an admin may still make one vanish-on-place: /zones place add <region> <id>); the build counts them
    and fails if one turns into a plain free-standing cube; its look is the vanilla Village Crate cube BY PATH: texture BlockTextures/Furniture_Village_Crate.png,
    icon Icons/ItemsGenerated/Furniture_Village_Crate.png - nothing vanilla is copied). Recipe: Workbench (Survival tab), 4 Ingredient_Stick
    -> 8. No tier (like stone / dirt) -> no tier tag, not in tools/tier_tags.py; no rarity -> Quality Common. Placed ONLY in a gathering
    area (a SKYBLOCK region or a whole-island gathering world with no region there), scaffold.on, the held id in the region's placeAllow
    (no line = the scaffold.ids row; none = nothing), the target cell air, all 6 neighbours gathering area too (never in or touching a
    town), nobody inside it, within scaffold.reach of the player's eyes, not a waiting spot. Our own Skyy_Scaffold item is refused
    everywhere else too ("Scaffolding can't go here." - it would never vanish there); builder mode places it anywhere (a normal block).
    Record first: a T journal line "T x y z <blockId> <vanishAt ms> <uuid>" (flushed) BEFORE the engine places it (the item is used up as
    usual; a refused place keeps it - probe Z5b). The 25th live one of a player makes that player's oldest vanish first. At vanishAt
    (scaffold.lifeSec 8 s) the cell is set to air ONLY if it still holds that block (no drop, no event - probe Z5); a cell changed meanwhile
    is left. A hand break (anyone, a mob too) is cancelled (no drop, no XP - Z19) and the scaffold goes at once; a hit may crack it. Each
    placement counts toward abuse.maxPerMin. Restart: every T line comes back and is removed at the first pass (its chunk loaded; unloaded
    = at chunk load). /zones restore all removes every scaffold (REQUIRED before a rollback: 0.3.0 skips T lines). A place another mod
    cancelled (the cell still air at the first pass) is forgotten. zones:fn:check answers deny for break / place on a live scaffold.
 2. SKILL GATES (Z4, spec 6.4): breaking / F-harvesting a listed block (and the tree trigger) can need a skill level: the per-type table
    (guard.properties gate.<type>=<Skill>,<Level>; Q1 defaults iron Mining 10; thorium, cobalt, lead, chromium 20; adamantite, slag 30;
    mithril, titanium 40; onyxium 45) and region.<id>.gate=Mining:10[,Foraging:5] (/zones region gate, or the regions table) - per skill the
    HIGHER of the two. A hit on a gated block gives no crack either. Levels: SkyySkills' bridge skill:fn:level (read only, cached 1 s per
    player + skill, a 0 never cached - fixer: a profile switch / a join before SkyySkills loaded shows within 1 s; never an edit of
    SkyySkills); no SkyySkills (-2) = gates off, warned once. Skill names: SkyySkills' own (checked at
    build against the pinned SkyySkills script); an unknown one is refused in Server Setup and by the command. Walking in is never stopped.
    "Requires Mining 10 (you: 7)."
 3. FAIR PLAY (Z4, spec 6.4; memory only, reset at restart; builder mode + zones.opBypass skip every rule; only resource breaks in gathering
    areas): A1 anti-AFK (anchor = where you were at the last break that moved more than abuse.afkRadius; still within it after abuse.afkSec
    900 s -> breaks refused until you are abuse.afkMove 8 blocks from the anchor; fixer: no break attempt for abuse.awaySec 300 s = you were
    away, not standing still -> a fresh anchor, so coming back to the same vein is never refused), A2 rate cap (abuse.maxPerMin 300 in a rolling minute;
    a second break by the same player in the same WORLD TICK - World.getTick, Vein Mine / Tree Feller extras - counts half; a felled tree
    counts as ONE break: its clearing breaks are never counted; over the cap -> refused abuse.rateRestSec 10 s, then a fresh minute; one
    admin log line), C2 turn limit (16-block patches; only while ANOTHER player broke in that patch within abuse.contestSec 60 s: more than
    abuse.cellCap 120 of your breaks there in abuse.cellWindowSec 600 s -> that patch refused for abuse.cellRestSec 60 s; solo never),
    C3 hit lock (a block another player hit within abuse.hitLockSec 3 s takes no damage / break from you - desk probe: block health is
    one BlockHealthSection per chunk section, damage(x, y, z, amount, time) has no player = SHARED, so the lock matters; 0 = off; fixer:
    a player the rules stopped - standing still, pausing after the cap, over the turn limit there - gets no crack and sets no lock, so
    nobody stopped can hold a block against others),
    A3 bot flag (after abuse.botSample 200 breaks, a gap spread under abuse.botGapMs 15 ms puts the player on /zones status "flagged" -
    never a punishment). Patches / hit marks / idle players are pruned every minute.
 4. COMMANDS (no new command: words of /zones, admin = skyyzones.admin checked in code like every admin word; the usage variants keep
    requirePermission(skyyzones.build) + setPermissionGroups(new String[0]) - HANDOFF section 3, lint perm_group_leaks): /zones region gate
    <region> <Skill:Level[,Skill:Level] or none>, /zones place add <region> <ids or look>, /zones place remove <region> <ids>; /zones info
    + "Scaffold: vanishes in N s", "Needs Mining 10 (you: 7)"; /zones status + scaffolds up, refused breaks in the last hour per reason
    (skill gate / standing still / too fast / turn limit / hit lock), flagged players (name + why), the biggest tree search.
 5. SERVER SETUP -> Zones (tools/skyycfg.py, KEEP=10): ONE new tab "Gates, scaffold, AFK" (fixer: the name shows all three; tab labels
    max 20) (scaffold.properties: scaffold.on / ids / lifeSec / maxPerPlayer / reach; guard.properties: gates.on, the gate table, abuse.*);
    to keep the tab count (Skyy 2026-10-16 "reduce and compress the menus") the 3 "Area titles" rows join "Builder tools" as "Titles +
    tools". Regions tab: a SECOND table "Region gates + placing" (rules[<region>] = "gate Mining:10; place ids|default|none", editable;
    spec "For the local session" 8: the regions cell itself stays as in 0.3.0 - with gate + place in it an ordinary region went over the
    200-character cell and could not be edited). New files are seeded once from the defaults - no migration.
 6. FINISHER FOLLOW-UPS (zones03): (a) ZFell.verify (a tree that grew back just before an unclean stop, written again) writes at most
    regen.passBatch blocks per pass like ZFell.write (cursor t.cur, the rest 50 ms later); (b) the cut-time tree search reads through a
    per-search chunk-section cache (one section lookup per 32^3 section, then the section's own palette) and its read cap is
    min(60,000, max(40,000, 10 x tree.maxBlocks)) - 60,000 at the default 6000 (was max(40,000, 30 x tree.maxBlocks) = 180,000 in one
    tick); a tree that needs more is refused like a too-big one ("too spread out" in the log); /zones status shows the biggest search.
    fixer: a tree refused as too big / too spread out is remembered for NEG_MS 15 s (key world + spot + tree.maxBlocks), so a held mouse
    never re-runs a 60,000-read search every hit; the tree.maxBlocks row says the read ceiling.
 7. FIXER (critics): a scaffold whose block id differs from the item id gets a fresh T line at its first pass (a restart then still finds
    it); scaffolds vanish BEFORE the regrow backlog in each pass (never late while a backlog fills regen.passBatch).
 8. FIXER 2 (second critics): (a) a locked (standing-still) player's HIT unlocks him once he is abuse.afkMove from the anchor (mining =
    hit then break; before, only a break - which a refused hit never reaches - could unlock); (b) placeable ids (scaffold.ids, /zones place
    add, the "Region gates + placing" table) must be PLAIN blocks - no block entity / bench / bed / seat / door / crop / states / F-use (a
    chest on a place list vanished with its contents); (c) the level cache carries profile:epoch:<uuid> (PROFILES-CONTRACT rule 2: a
    switch reads fresh at once), so a 0 is cached 1 s too; SkyySkills' -1 (unknown skill name) = that skill's gate off, -2 = every gate
    off, each warned once (was clamped to 0 = refused for good); (d) the 5-minute "away" gap is the Server Setup row abuse.awaySec (300 s);
    (e) a refused HIT counts once a second per player + reason on /zones status (a held mouse fires many); (f) zones.on off no longer
    lets our Scaffolding become a permanent block - its rules still apply (fail closed); (g) a zone reset keeps the zone's scaffolds as T
    lines in the reset backup and its undo takes them back FORCED (the first pass clears each one still standing) - no scaffold comes back
    permanent; (h) msg.gapSec's help says it spaces every refusal note. Left: NEG_MS 15 s stays internal (an anti-lag memory, not a
    tuning value; a tree.maxBlocks change is part of its key, so a new cap applies at once).
 UNVERIFIED (needs the game; spec probes P4-P6 were never run): the Village Crate cube as scaffolding (stand on it: yes, a solid cube;
 climbable: no - pillar up with it); a scaffold placed by the engine has the item's block id; World.getTick is the same for a Vein Mine
 extra as for its hand break; the real cost of a 60,000-read search with the section cache (expected a few ms); what a 0.3.0 rollback
 shows for Skyy_Scaffold items in inventories.
 ROLLBACK to 0.3.0 (fixer 2: if scaffolding is the ONLY problem, do NOT roll back - set Server Setup -> Zones -> Gates, scaffold, AFK ->
 "Scaffolding in gathering areas" OFF: every scaffold goes at once, new ones are refused, no item becomes unknown; gates / fair play have
 their own off rows): (1) tell players to drop / use up their Scaffolding (inventories, chests, the ground): 0.3.0 does not know the
 Skyy_Scaffold item (unverified what the engine does with an unknown item - assume it is lost); (2) break by hand every Scaffolding block
 placed in builder mode or by a zones.opBypass admin (those are normal blocks, never timed, so /zones restore all does not see them);
 (3) /zones restore all (removes every timed scaffold), wait until /zones status shows "0 up now", stop the server. scaffold.properties /
 guard.properties may stay (0.3.0 ignores them); 0.3.0 counts T lines as bad lines; the region gate / placeAllow lines stay (0.3.0 keeps them
 verbatim).
"""
import os, sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, "tools"))
import soundpass_gen as G

P = G.Patch(os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyZones", "build_skyyzones_0.3.0.py"), os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyZones", "build_skyyzones_0.3.1.py"))
